    "Scarcity": {"Explanation": "The email creates urgency by stating 'we need a short, looping animation showcasing the new \u2018NovaBoost\u2019 feature.  It\u2019s vital for the upcoming social media push and needs to be ready by end of day tomorrow', implying a limited time frame for action."},
    "Authority": {"Explanation": "The email references the sender's authority as a 'Senior Marketing Strategist' at BrightTech, which could lend credibility and authority to the request."},
    "Commitment/Consistency": {"Explanation": "The email references prior behavior, mentioning the recipient's past work ('your expertise in animations and animatronics \u2013 and your impressive work at BrightTech over the last two years \u2013 I immediately thought of you'), which could prompt the recipient to commit to helping again."},
    "Liking": {"Explanation": "The email uses personalization and flattery ('I immediately thought of you') to build a positive relationship and rapport with the recipient."},
    "Social proof": {"Explanation": "Not present"}
}

